        "original_id": "b8c18187-06dc-5d45-8e0d-7f38de4144d7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Manning Field at John L. Guidry Stadium\n- People: Eli Manning, Peyton Manning, Archie Manning, David Tyree, Philip Rivers\n- Organizations: New York Giants, San Diego Chargers, National Football League\n- Events: Manning Passing Academy, 2004 NFL Draft, Super Bowl XLII, Helmet Catch\n- Roles: quarterback, wide receiver\n\nFacts:\n- Manning Field at John L. Guidry Stadium has its playing surface named Manning Field after the Manning family.\n- Peyton Manning, Eli Manning, and Archie Manning hold the Manning Passing Academy football camp at Manning Field at John L. Guidry Stadium.\n- Eli Manning was born on January 3, 1981.\n- Eli Manning is an American football quarterback for the New York Giants of the National Football League.\n- Eli Manning was drafted first overall by the San Diego Chargers in the 2004 NFL Draft and was immediately traded to the New York Giants in exchange for a package highlighted by the fourth overall pick, Philip Rivers.\n- On February 3, 2008, the Helmet Catch was an American football play in the final two minutes of Super Bowl XLII involving New York Giants quarterback Eli Manning and wide receiver David Tyree.",
